lesson: 238
title: Board games
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: A chess game starts with 32 pieces on the board, 16 white and 16 black.
explain: Each capture takes one piece off the board, so subtract all the captures of both players from 32.
explain: White has taken 5 pieces and Black 3: 32 − 5 − 3 = 24 pieces are still on the board.
vars: a=name c=name x=1..12 y=1..12 k=20..60
answer: 32 - x - y
exercise: In a game of chess, White has taken {x} pieces and Black has taken {y} pieces. How many pieces are still on the board?
exercise: {a} and {c} play chess. {a} captures {x} pieces and {c} captures {y}. How many pieces are left on the board?
exercise: How many chess pieces are on the board after {x} captures by White and {y} by Black?
exercise: In a chess game at school, {x} white pieces and {y} black pieces have been taken. How many pieces are still on the board?
exercise: {a} is winning at chess: {a.he} has captured {x} pieces, and {c} has captured {y}. How many pieces are on the board now?
exercise: chess, i took {x} of his, he took {y} of mine. how many pieces left on the board
exercise: {a} took {x+1}, no wait {x} pieces, and {c} took {y}. how many still on the board
exercise: me n grandad playing chess, he's taken {y} of mine, i've taken {x}, oh and the cat knocked one off but we put it back. how many on the board
exercise: my friend says {64-x-y} pieces left cos 64 squares lol. nah, {x} n {y} captured. how many left
exercise: chess game, white lost {y}, black lost {x}. pieces left on board
test: After Black loses {x} pieces and White loses {y}, how many pieces remain on the board?
test: What number of chess pieces are still in play once the two players have captured {x} and {y} pieces?
test: {x} n {y} pieces taken in chess so far, how many still on the board
test: {c} has won {y} of {a}'s pieces and {a} has won {x} of {c}'s. Count the pieces left on the board.
test: chess, {x} captures for me {y} for her. whats left on the board
test: After {k} moves, White has captured {x} pieces and Black {y}. How many pieces are on the board?
exam: Determine the number of pieces remaining upon the chessboard subsequent to the capture of {x.words} pieces by White and {y.words} pieces by Black, the game having commenced from the standard initial position.
exam: It is given that, in a game of chess begun from the customary starting arrangement, {x} pieces have been captured by one player and {y} by the other. Ascertain the number of pieces still in play.
exam: Compute the quantity of chess pieces present on the board, whereas {a} has captured {x} and {c} has captured {y}.
exam: State the number of pieces extant on the board after White has effected {x} captures and Black {y} captures in a game of chess.
exercise: The late Mr Brown's chess set is still complete. {a} and {c} play with it: {a} takes {x} pieces and {c} takes {y}. How many pieces are left on the board?
exercise: {c} had to go and powder {c.his} nose mid-game and the git didn't move a thing while {c.he} was gone. {a} had taken {x} pieces, {c} had taken {y}. how many pieces left on the board?
test: {a}'s grandfather, who went to meet his maker last year, played {k} games on this board. In today's game White has captured {x} pieces and Black {y}. How many pieces are still standing?
